{"stage": "sc", "served_model": "gpt-4.1-2025-04-14", "status": "completed", "usage": {"input_tokens": 2101, "input_tokens_details": {"cache_write_tokens": 0, "cached_tokens": 1920, "cache_write_tokens_details": {"ttl_12h_tokens": 0, "ttl_30m_tokens": 0}}, "output_tokens": 492, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 0}, "total_tokens": 2593}, "output": [{"id": "msg_029a5007f100da1d006afce895ffb087d092167da00e3a46e2", "content": [{"annotations": [], "text": "#### Summary of findings:\n\n- **Goal:** Best possible energy resolution at 100 GeV.\n- **Candidates:** Absorber-F1, Absorber-F2, Absorber-F3; all mechanically feasible and machinable in range 2\u201310 mm.\n- **Hands-on maintenance:** No absorber option prohibits access.\n- **Simulation results (energy resolution, lower is better):**\n    - **Absorber-F2:** Best results at 6 mm (3.10%) and 5 mm (3.21%), with a small change between 4\u20137 mm. Thinner plates (<4 mm) degrade performance, as do much thicker ones.\n    - **Absorber-F3:** Consistently worse than F2 by ~0.6% across all thicknesses.\n    - **Absorber-F1:** Worst; 5.1\u20137.2% (both thicker and thinner plates worsen result).\n\n#### Next steps:\n- Prepare final recommendation for Absorber-F2 at 6 mm thickness, with a justification and explicit check against all requirements.", "type": "output_text", "logprobs": []}], "role": "assistant", "status": "completed", "type": "message", "phase": null}, {"arguments": "{\"option\":\"Absorber-F2\",\"plate_mm\":6,\"justification\":\"Absorber-F2 at 6 mm provides the best simulated energy resolution at 100 GeV (3.10%) compared to other materials and thicknesses. It is compatible with hands-on maintenance and mechanical tolerances. No other candidate or thickness matches this performance within project constraints.\",\"requirements\":[{\"requirement\":\"The absorber must be one of the three materials listed in candidate_specs.md.\",\"status\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"Absorber-F2 is listed as a candidate material in candidate_specs.md.\"},{\"requirement\":\"The calorimeter must allow hands-on maintenance during shutdowns.\",\"status\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"No project document or meeting note indicates any absorber interferes with maintenance; all are compatible with the support design.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Plate thickness between 2 and 10 mm.\",\"status\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"Recommendation uses 6 mm plate thickness, which is inside the allowed range.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Achieve the best possible energy resolution at 100 GeV.\",\"status\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"Geant4 simulations show Absorber-F2 at 6 mm gives the best energy resolution (3.10%) among tested candidates and thicknesses.\"}]}", "call_id": "call_OUrv9IINglLUxiGRkWlDNJZo", "name": "submit_recommendation", "type": "function_call", "id": "fc_029a5007f100da1d006afce897f09087d09ed26c67bfb1e98a", "async_": null, "caller": null, "namespace": null, "status": "completed"}]}
